<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Definitions xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
	<EntityComponents>

<!-- Cargo Ship Route Arrival - Unload & Despawn
     For the fixed-route Nautical-path cargo ships in Paths-Nautical.sbc (WW2-Behavior-CargoShip-
     {Gray/Green}-{Anchor}-{Anchor}), NOT the ambient single-destination ships in
     Behaviors-CargoShip.sbc (those already have their own DestinationReached flow via
     Triggers-Destination_Ship.sbc).

     Verified against MES source (Data/Scripts/ModularEncountersSystems/Behavior/CargoShip.cs):
     [BehaviorName:Nautical] does NOT support [CustomWaypoints:...] at all - that tag only exists
     on the CargoShip behavior subclass. Paths-Nautical.sbc's 8 route Behaviors were declaring
     [BehaviorName:Nautical] + [CustomWaypoints:...] together, so the waypoint list was being
     silently ignored (Nautical is a pure target-seeking combat behavior with no waypoint concept
     at all). Fixed alongside this file: all 8 legs switched to [BehaviorName:CargoShip].

     Under CargoShip, every waypoint in the list (including the last) briefly pauses the ship in
     WaitAtWaypoint mode - governed by the ship's own AutopilotData's [WaypointWaitTimeTrigger]
     (WW2-Autopilot-CargoShip already has this at 15s, unchanged), firing BehaviorTriggerA - then
     auto-resumes toward the next point with NO trigger action required to advance. Once the
     CustomWaypoints list is exhausted, the ship fires BehaviorTriggerD exactly once, at the final
     waypoint's position, immediately before it would otherwise peel off toward an auto-generated
     despawn coordinate and vanish out at sea. This is the hook used below: freeze the ship in
     place right there (so it looks like it's sitting at the dock, not drifting off-route), run the
     5-minute unload wait, then despawn in place instead of letting MES's own silent despawn logic
     carry it away first.

     Delivery scoring: each route Behavior in Paths-Nautical.sbc lists its own WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-{Route}
     (+100 to the destination anchor, Territory-Points.sbc), a 5-min timer enabled by BeginUnload below.

     Gravity/roll-over note: does NOT use DisableAutopilot on arrival. Per MES source
     (Behavior/Subsystems/AutoPilot/AutoPilotSystem.cs), DisableAutopilot calls
     DeactivateAutoPilot(), which stops ALL gyro override including FlyLevelWithGravity leveling -
     on a boat that relies on active gyro leveling rather than passive keel/buoyancy stability,
     that would let it drift and roll during the 5-minute parked wait. Instead this only kills
     current spin (StopAllRotation) and zeroes forward speed (ChangeAutopilotSpeed:0), leaving the
     autopilot itself engaged so it keeps calling ApplyAutopilot()/ApplyGyroRotation() every tick -
     FlyLevelWithGravity (already true on WW2-Autopilot-CargoShip) keeps actively leveling the
     whole time it's parked. Also added [LevelWithGravityWhenIdle:true] to WW2-Autopilot-CargoShip
     as a defensive second layer, in case the ship is ever fully idle rather than just parked at
     zero speed. -->

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Trigger-CargoShip-RouteArrived</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Trigger]
			[UseTrigger:true]
			[Type:BehaviorTriggerD]
			[StartsReady:true]
			[MaxActions:1]
			[Actions:WW2-Territory-Action-CargoShip-BeginUnload]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Action-CargoShip-BeginUnload</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Action]

			[StopAllRotation:true]
			[ChangeAutopilotSpeed:true]
			[NewAutopilotSpeed:0]

			[UseChatBroadcast:true]
			[ChatData:WW2-Territory-Chat-CargoShip-Arrived]

			[ResetCooldownTimeOfTriggers:true]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-CargoShip-UnloadTimer]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-LaSpezia-Tripoli]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-Tripoli-LaSpezia]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-LaSpezia-Civitavecchia]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-Civitavecchia-LaSpezia]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Oran-Toulon]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Toulon-Oran]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Toulon-Alexandria]
			[ResetTriggerCooldownNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Alexandria-Toulon]

			[EnableTriggers:true]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-CargoShip-UnloadTimer]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-LaSpezia-Tripoli]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-Tripoli-LaSpezia]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-LaSpezia-Civitavecchia]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Gray-Civitavecchia-LaSpezia]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Oran-Toulon]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Toulon-Oran]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Toulon-Alexandria]
			[EnableTriggerNames:WW2-Territory-Trigger-Delivery-Green-Alexandria-Toulon]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Chat-CargoShip-Arrived</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Chat]
			[UseChat:true]
			[StartsReady:true]
			[MaxChats:1]
			[BroadcastRandomly:true]
			[Author:Cargo Ship Pilot]
			[Color:Red]
			[IgnoreAntennaRequirement:true]
			[IgnoredAntennaRangeOverride:3000]

			[ChatMessages:{AntennaName} has arrived and begun unloading cargo.]
			[ChatAudio:ArcHudGPSNotification1]
			[BroadcastChatType:Chat]

			[ChatMessages:Dockhands are unloading {AntennaName} now.]
			[ChatAudio:ArcHudGPSNotification1]
			[BroadcastChatType:Chat]

			[ChatMessages:{AntennaName} moored, cargo transfer underway.]
			[ChatAudio:ArcHudGPSNotification1]
			[BroadcastChatType:Chat]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

<!-- 5-minute unload wait, then despawn in place. 5s after the route's delivery timer so points land first. -->
		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Trigger-CargoShip-UnloadTimer</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Trigger]
			[UseTrigger:false]
			[Type:Timer]
			[MinCooldownMs:305000]
			[MaxCooldownMs:305001]
			[StartsReady:false]
			[MaxActions:1]
			[Actions:WW2-Territory-Action-CargoShip-FinishUnload]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Action-CargoShip-FinishUnload</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Action]

			[UseChatBroadcast:true]
			[ChatData:WW2-Territory-Chat-CargoShip-Departed]

			[SetBooleansTrue:Retired]
			[ForceDespawn:true]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>

		<EntityComponent xsi:type="MyObjectBuilder_InventoryComponentDefinition">
			<Id>
				<TypeId>Inventory</TypeId>
				<SubtypeId>WW2-Territory-Chat-CargoShip-Departed</SubtypeId>
			</Id>
			<Description>

			[RivalAI Chat]
			[UseChat:true]
			[StartsReady:true]
			[MaxChats:1]
			[BroadcastRandomly:true]
			[Author:Cargo Ship Pilot]
			[Color:Red]
			[IgnoreAntennaRequirement:true]
			[IgnoredAntennaRangeOverride:3000]

			[ChatMessages:{AntennaName} unloading complete, casting off.]
			[ChatAudio:ArcHudGPSNotification1]
			[BroadcastChatType:Chat]

			[ChatMessages:Cargo transfer finished. {AntennaName} departing port.]
			[ChatAudio:ArcHudGPSNotification1]
			[BroadcastChatType:Chat]

			</Description>
		</EntityComponent>
	<!-- End Cargo Ship Route Arrival -->

	</EntityComponents>
</Definitions>
